Let's see. Elves can be priests, rangers and wizards. A ranger would
usually wield a bow or an elven dagger or broadsword. Thrown daggers are
not a problem, so they're good to go. Priests don't even have a non-iron
starting weapon. They could use unihorns, though. But until they get one,
they'd be basically weaponless. Wizards would use their staff and throw
daggers, maybe wield an elven dagger. No MagicBane, though, that's a
problem.

I found the following non-iron artefact weapons: The Staff, Sting, Orcrist,
Grayswandir and Werebane. The Staff, being an intelligent neutral quest
artefact, is right out. Sting and Orcrist are laughable. Grayswandir is an
option, but hard to get. Most notably, Stormbringer, which would be a
typical weapon for an elf in NetHack, is made of iron.

So you'd probably want to make it an option, to emphasize a "no iron
weapon" roleplaying conduct. It would be most easily achievable with
wizards and rangers. Wizards would have to use an elven dagger as their
melee weapon in the late game, and rangers might have a big stack of
daggers and an enchanted elven broadsword.


